# rule_stomp (2026-11-18; decision log D92/D93, standard BOOK 02-architecture/STANDARD-RULES-AS-OPS-FOUNDATION-DESIGN-2026-11-18.md): the STOMP / HIT contact rule as an op. _shared-lib/rule_stomp.c is the pure module (called in-process by the game tick loop, targets are rule_patrol.c walkers), ops/rule_stomp_op.c is its CLI face.
# Every pinned number is HAND-COMPUTED. Bodies are 200 x 200 Q8, the walker stands at x 1000, y 568 (its head at y 568), margin 64: a stomp needs  (hero y + 200) - vy  <=  568 + 64 = 632. Sabotage-proven (see the commit message).
RESULTS | ../results/rule_stomp.txt
ENV | LC_ALL | C

CASE    | setup
SCRATCH |
RUN | /bin/cp | $HOUSE/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/rule_stomp_op.+x | $T/rs
EXPECT_EXISTS | rs | the-real-op-is-built
WRITE | stomp.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | edge632.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 472 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | edge633.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 473 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | rising.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p -10\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | still.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p 0\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | side.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 900 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 0\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | apart.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1300 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | touching.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 800 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | dead.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 0
WRITE | two.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1\nWALKER \p 1050 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | margin0.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 0\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 472 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | margin100.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 100\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 480 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | data.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 100\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 250\nHERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | norule.pdl | HERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | standing_above.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 400 \p 200 \p 200 \p 0\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1
WRITE | hitfirst.pdl | RULE \p stomp_margin \p 64\nRULE \p stomp_bounce \p 133\nRULE \p stomp_score \p 100\nHERO \p 1000 \p 460 \p 200 \p 200 \p 40\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 400 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1\nWALKER \p 1000 \p 568 \p 200 \p 200 \p 1

CASE    | stomp
# the hero (y 460, falling 40) overlaps the walker (y 568 to 768): (460 + 200) - 40 = 620 <= 632, so it is a STOMP: the walker dies, vy = -133, +100
RUN | $T/rs | $T/stomp.pdl
EXPECT_EXIT | 0 | the-op-runs
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 1 HIT 0 SCORE 100 HERO vy=-133 WALKERS=0 | HAND-COMPUTED-620-<=-632-a-stomp-the-walker-dies-and-the-hero-bounces

CASE    | the-exact-boundary
# (y + 200) - 40 against 632: y 472 gives 632 (<=, a stomp), y 473 gives 633 (a HIT)
RUN | $T/rs | $T/edge632.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 1 HIT 0 SCORE 100 HERO vy=-133 WALKERS=0 | HAND-COMPUTED-632-<=-632-still-a-stomp
RUN | $T/rs | $T/edge633.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 1 SCORE 0 HERO vy=40 WALKERS=1 | HAND-COMPUTED-633-is-too-deep-so-it-is-a-HIT-and-the-walker-lives

CASE    | not-a-stomp
# rising (vy -10) and standing (vy 0) are hits even from above; a side touch is a hit
RUN | $T/rs | $T/rising.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 1 SCORE 0 HERO vy=-10 WALKERS=1 | HAND-COMPUTED-rising-is-a-hit
RUN | $T/rs | $T/still.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 1 SCORE 0 HERO vy=0 WALKERS=1 | HAND-COMPUTED-vy-0-is-a-hit
RUN | $T/rs | $T/side.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 1 SCORE 0 HERO vy=0 WALKERS=1 | HAND-COMPUTED-a-side-touch-x-900-to-1100-over-1000-to-1200-is-a-hit

CASE    | no-contact
# apart (x 1300, past the walker's right edge 1200) and only edge-touching (x 800 + 200 = 1000: the overlap is strict) do nothing, even while falling; a dead walker is ignored
RUN | $T/rs | $T/apart.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 0 SCORE 0 HERO vy=40 WALKERS=1 | HAND-COMPUTED-no-overlap-nothing-happens
RUN | $T/rs | $T/touching.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 0 SCORE 0 HERO vy=40 WALKERS=1 | HAND-COMPUTED-edges-that-only-touch-do-not-overlap
RUN | $T/rs | $T/dead.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 0 SCORE 0 HERO vy=40 WALKERS=0 | HAND-COMPUTED-a-dead-walker-is-ignored-(no-stomp-no-hit)

CASE    | two-walkers
# a stomp turns vy into a rise, so a SECOND overlapping walker in the same tick is a HIT (the existing behaviour, kept): the first walker is stomped (+100), then the hit ends the scan
RUN | $T/rs | $T/two.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 1 HIT 1 SCORE 100 HERO vy=-133 WALKERS=01 | HAND-COMPUTED-first-stomped-second-is-a-hit

CASE    | the-numbers-are-data
# stomp_margin 0: 632 <= 568 is false, so y 472 is a HIT; stomp_margin 100: (480 + 200) - 40 = 640 <= 668, a STOMP; stomp_bounce 100 gives vy -100 and stomp_score 250 gives SCORE 250
RUN | $T/rs | $T/margin0.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 1 | HAND-COMPUTED-margin-0-the-same-contact-is-now-a-hit
RUN | $T/rs | $T/margin100.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 1 HIT 0 SCORE 100 | HAND-COMPUTED-margin-100-a-deeper-stomp-counts
RUN | $T/rs | $T/data.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 1 HIT 0 SCORE 250 HERO vy=-100 WALKERS=0 | HAND-COMPUTED-bounce-100-and-score-250-come-from-the-RULE-rows

CASE    | contract
RUN | $T/rs | --describe
EXPECT_OUT | RULE keys: stomp_margin stomp_bounce stomp_score | the-op-describes-its-inputs-outputs-and-RULE-keys
RUN | $T/rs | $T/norule.pdl
EXPECT_EXIT | 2 | NEGATIVE-a-scene-without-the-three-RULE-numbers-is-refused
EXPECT_OUT | the numbers are data, there is no default | and-the-op-says-why

CASE    | falling-is-required
# a hero resting just above (y 400 to 600, vy 0) overlaps the walker head (568) by 32 and its feet term (400 + 200) - 0 = 600 <= 632 WOULD pass the depth test: only vy > 0 makes it a HIT. A falling-only rule is what stops a hero that is standing or rising from killing by touch
RUN | $T/rs | $T/standing_above.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 1 SCORE 0 HERO vy=0 WALKERS=1 | HAND-COMPUTED-not-falling-so-a-HIT-although-the-depth-test-alone-would-pass

CASE    | a-hit-stops-the-scan
# the hero (y 460, falling 40) overlaps walker A (y 400: (660 - 40) = 620 <= 464 is false, a HIT) and then walker B (the standard one, a stomp). The hit ENDS the scan, so B is NOT stomped: WALKERS=11, vy stays 40
RUN | $T/rs | $T/hitfirst.pdl
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 0 HIT 1 SCORE 0 HERO vy=40 WALKERS=11 | HAND-COMPUTED-the-first-contact-is-a-hit-and-the-scan-stops-before-the-second-walker

CASE    | event-page
# the rule is on the house's event vocabulary and in a Blueprintz page (D93, recipe in the standard section 12): a registry COMMAND row, the page tm_stomp (seeded through the real events-hq manager), whose compiled wrapper runs THIS op with the page's parameter
RUN | grep | -c | ^COMMAND rule_stomp$ | $HOUSE/#.ref/menu/event_commands.registry.pdl
EXPECT_OUT_IS | 1 | the-registry-has-exactly-one-COMMAND-rule_stomp-row
EXPECT_HAS | $HOUSE/@.apps/teario/events/tm_stomp/event_pkg/pages/page_1/event.ir.pdl | type=rule_stomp | the-page-command-is-the-registered-type
EXPECT_HAS | $HOUSE/@.apps/teario/events/tm_stomp/event_pkg/pages/page_1/condition.pdl | COND \p trigger \p ui | the-page-has-a-trigger
RUN | sh | $HOUSE/@.apps/teario/events/tm_stomp/event_pkg/pages/page_1/cmd_1.sh
EXPECT_EXIT | 0 | the-compiled-wrapper-runs-the-op
EXPECT_OUT | STOMPS 1 HIT 0 SCORE 100 HERO vy=-133 WALKERS=0 | the-page-gives-the-SAME-line-as-the-op-alone-(the-stomp)
